  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Second-order derivative"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Differentiating $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ again gives $\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}$, also written $y''$ or $y_2$. For example, if $y = A\\sin x + B\\cos x$ then $y'' = -y$.",
    "kn": "dy/dx ಅನ್ನು ಮತ್ತೆ ಅವಕಲಿಸಿದರೆ ದ್ವಿತೀಯ ಕ್ರಮದ ಅವಕಲಜ d²y/dx² ಸಿಗುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "y'' = d/dx (dy/dx)"
    },
    {
     "en": "y = A sin x + B cos x ⇒ y'' + y = 0"
    },
    {
     "en": "y = e^(mx) ⇒ y'' = m² e^(mx)"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Differentiate the first derivative once more to get the second derivative, d two y by d x squared.",
    "kn": "dy/dx ಅನ್ನು ಮತ್ತೆ ಅವಕಲಿಸಿದರೆ ದ್ವಿತೀಯ ಕ್ರಮದ ಅವಕಲಜ d²y/dx² ಸಿಗುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "formula": "\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right)"
  },
